// Chapter 2 — the trail. River checks converge before an optional night-camp hub.

=== trail.river
@title The River

{image("river-crossing.jpg", "A rope stretches across a swollen jungle river toward an ancient green stone stair on the opposite bank.")}

The trail ends at a brown river, swollen with last night's rain. On the far bank, through the trees, you
can make out a stair of green stone.

* [Tie off the rope and cross carefully] (requires: player has rope) { player:xp += 25 } -> trail.far-bank
* [Swim for it] skill-check athletics dc 12
  success: -> trail.far-bank
  failure: { player:hp -= 3 } -> trail.swept
* [Let {guide:first-name} find a ford] skill-check guide survival dc 13
  success: -> trail.far-bank
  failure: { player:hp -= 1 } -> trail.swept

=== trail.swept
The current takes your legs out from under you. You claw your way onto the far bank a long way downstream,
coughing up river and dignity in equal measure.
{if player:hp < 8}
You are bleeding from a gash along your arm.
{/if}
-> trail.far-bank

=== trail.far-bank
{guide:first-name} squelches up the bank behind you and stares up at the stair.

> guide: Well, {player:first-name}. It's real.

* [Make camp before the climb] -> trail.night
* [Climb straight to the temple] -> temple.door

=== trail.night
@title The Night Watch
@hub any(night,watch)
@hub-limit 1

{image("night-watch.jpeg", "A low fire lights an expedition awning and a brass tripwire bell at the foot of a jungle stair.")}

You shelter beneath a canvas awning at the foot of the stair. {guide:first-name}
hangs a bell on a tripwire and spreads the expedition records across a rough table.
Beyond the firelight, the jungle never quite falls silent.

* [Press on at dawn] -> temple.door

=== trail.supper
@title Eat a ration
@tags night
@requires player has ration
@priority 20
@once

You open the pack and unwrap a {item:ration} for supper.

* [Share supper by the fire] { take player ration; clear flag:packing-open }
-> trail.supper-done

=== trail.supper-done
@title A Quiet Meal

{if not flag:packing-open and player has ration}
You close the pack with one ration left, safely stowed for tomorrow.
{/if}
{guide:first-name} takes the empty wrappers. The fire burns low.

-> trail.night

=== trail.jaguar
@title Stand your ground
@tags night
@requires not visited(trail.jaguar)
@priority 10
@once

~ player:courage += 10

{image("jaguar.jpeg", "A watchful jaguar emerges from wet foliage at the edge of the campfire's light.")}

A jaguar steps out of the brush. You hold its gaze until it turns aside,
leaving you trembling but upright. Your Courage is **{player:courage}**.

{if flag:steady}
{guide:first-name} lowers the machete. "Steady. That's how we get home."
{/if}
{if player:courage >= 6}
~ player:xp += 5
{/if}

* [Catch your breath] -> trail.night

=== trail.signal
@title Follow the signal
@tags night
@requires visited(trail.jaguar) and player:courage >= 6
@priority 10
@once

Something whistles from beyond the fire. {guide:first-name} is nowhere in sight.
The answer in your ledger is "{var:watch-note}"; tonight's watchword is "{var:watchword}".

{if var:watchword != "" and var:watchword == var:watch-note}
You call the phrase you agreed on. A familiar voice answers.
-> trail.found
{/if}
-> trail.wait

=== trail.found
@title A Familiar Voice

{guide:first-name} steps into the light with an armful of dry wood.
The watchword has done its job.

-> trail.night

=== trail.wait
@title Stay in the Light

The ledger cannot answer for you. You stay beside the fire until {guide:first-name}
returns, and agree not to follow a voice you cannot place.

-> trail.night

=== trail.bell
@title Check the tripwire bell
@tags trail,watch
@requires visited(trail.signal)
@priority -1
@once

The watch bell has sounded **{var:bell-count}** times. A low branch is caught
in the tripwire. You can lift it clear, then check whether the line still holds.

* [Ring the bell] (requires: not flag:bell-ringing) { set flag:bell-ringing } -> trail.bell
* [Silence the bell] (requires: flag:bell-ringing) { clear flag:bell-ringing } -> trail.bell
* [Return to the fire] { clear flag:bell-ringing } -> trail.night
